unit Kafka.SaslConnectionTests;

{$mode delphi}{$H+}

{ GENERATED FILE — produced by tools/gen_fpc_mirror.py from
  tests/Unit/Kafka.SaslConnectionTests.pas (DUnitX). Do not edit by hand: edit the DUnitX
  master and run the script again. }

{ Tests for SASL inside Kafka.Connection's Open, against the in-process fake
  broker (Kafka.TestFakeBroker), whose SCRAM side is a server's, written
  apart from Kafka.Sasl's client.

  - PLAIN, SCRAM-SHA-256 and SCRAM-SHA-512 with the right credentials:
    Open authenticates after ApiVersions and Metadata works; SCRAM with a
    user name that needs escaping and a non-ASCII password; SCRAM over TLS
    (SASL_SSL). SCRAM-SHA-512's wrong password, wrong server signature and
    a broker that enables only SCRAM-SHA-256.
  - Failures are EKafkaAuthentication with the broker's code: a wrong
    password and an unknown user (SASL_AUTHENTICATION_FAILED, the broker's
    message, never the password), a mechanism the broker doesn't enable
    (UNSUPPORTED_SASL_MECHANISM, with the ones it does), a listener without
    SASL (ILLEGAL_SASL_STATE), and a broker whose SCRAM signature is wrong
    (code 0: the client's own check). The connection is closed afterwards.
  - A client without SASL on a SASL listener: Open (ApiVersions) works, and
    the broker hangs up on the first other request (EKafkaConnection).
  - KIP-368: the session lifetime the broker gives is kept; with none, or a
    long one, ReauthenticationDue stays False; with 1 ms it is due at once.
  - The cluster with wrong credentials raises EKafkaAuthentication at once,
    not EKafkaConnection after MaxBlockMs; a producer delivers through a
    SASL broker.
  - OAUTHBEARER: the provider's token and the extensions reach the broker,
    in plaintext and over TLS; a token the broker refuses is
    EKafkaAuthentication with SASL_AUTHENTICATION_FAILED and the broker's
    JSON (in the message and as BrokerMessage), never the token; no
    provider, a provider that raises and a token that isn't a bearer token
    fail before anything is sent past ApiVersions. The provider is asked at
    each connection: two connections, two tokens; a cluster whose sessions
    are due at once (KIP-368) hands out a new connection each time, each
    with a new token; and a producer delivers through it.

  DUnitX master: the FPCUnit mirror in tests/Unit/fpc is generated by
  tools/gen_fpc_mirror.py. }

